    "title": "Kerr quasinormal mode frequencies and excitation factors",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14380191",
    "publication_date": "2025-02-19",
    "description": "<p>Kerr quasinormal mode frequencies and excitation factors for gravitational ($s=-2$), electromagnetic ($s=-1$), and scalar fields ($s=0$). &nbsp;Normalization is $2M=1$ except for the spin parameter $a/M$.</p>\n<h2>Data Format</h2>\n<p>$a/M$, $\\mathrm{Re}(2M\\omega)$, $\\mathrm{Im}(2M\\omega)$, $\\mathrm{Re}(A)$, $\\mathrm{Im}(A)$, $\\mathrm{Re}(\\nu)$, $\\mathrm{Im}(\\nu)$, $\\mathrm{Re}((2M)^{-2s}B)$, $\\mathrm{Im}((2M)^{-2s}B)$</p>\n<p>$M$: Mass<br>$a$: Spin parameter<br>$\\omega$: Quasinormal mode frequency<br>$A$: Separation constant<br>$\\nu$: Renormalized angular momentum<br>$B$: Excitation factor</p>\n<h2>How to cite</h2>\n<p>If you use this dataset, please cite both this Zenodo record and the associated publication.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For the Zenodo record, the following BibTeX entry uses the DOI that represents all versions, and resolves to the latest version of the dataset:</p>\n<pre class=\"language-markup\"><code>@misc{motohashi_2024_12696857,\n  author       = {Motohashi, Hayato},\n  title        = {Kerr quasinormal mode frequencies and excitation factors},\n  month        = jul,\n  year         = 2024,\n  publisher    = {Zenodo},\n  doi          = {10.5281/zenodo.12696857},\n  url          = {https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.12696857},\n}</code></pre>\n<p>For a version-specific citation, please use the citation information provided by Zenodo.</p>\n<p>Associated publication:</p>\n<pre class=\"language-markup\"><code>@article{Motohashi:2024fwt,\n    author = \"Motohashi, Hayato\",\n    title = \"{Resonant Excitation of Quasinormal Modes of Black Holes}\",\n    eprint = \"2407.15191\",\n    archivePrefix = \"arXiv\",\n    primaryClass = \"gr-qc\",\n    doi = \"10.1103/PhysRevLett.134.141401\",\n    journal = \"Phys. Rev. Lett.\",\n    volume = \"134\",\n    number = \"14\",\n    pages = \"141401\",\n    year = \"2025\"\n}</code></pre>\n<h2>Version History</h2>\n<p>Version 0.2.0: Expanded dataset with additional modes:&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; $s=-2$, $\\ell=4&ndash;6$, $n=0&ndash;7$&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; $s=-1$, $\\ell=2&ndash;6$, $n=0&ndash;7$<br>&nbsp; $s=0$, $\\ell=1&ndash;6$, $n=0&ndash;7$<br>Version 0.1.1: Added GIF animation (no changes to dataset)<br>Version 0.1.0: Initial release with $s=-2$, $\\ell=2&ndash;3$, $n=0&ndash;7$</p>",
